  {
   "id": 1,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    0,
    -330
   ],
   "size": [
    740,
    290
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 0,
   "mode": 0,
   "title": "Terrain -> AI texture (read me first)",
   "properties": {
    "text": ""
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "A complete procedural terrain -> diffusion model -> back onto the mesh chain.\n\n1) The two left columns are the terrain: noise -> stream power erosion (cuts river valleys) -> erosion filter -> thermal erosion -> hydraulic erosion (gullies + sediment, accumulated into debris) -> flow accumulation (rivers, lakes) -> Splat Map (grass / sediment / rock / snow / water, the five layers sum to 1 everywhere).\n2) Regional Prompt writes prompts per splat-layer region (one per line, later lines take priority); Control Image's height mode outputs a top-down depth map (high = white).\n3) SDXL + union ControlNet (depth) produces a top-down texture aligned pixel for pixel with the height field.\n4) COP Import reads the texture back into COP, Composite puts it into the terrain's albedo layer, HeightField to Mesh outputs a mesh with Cd=albedo, Geometry Preview's color mode shows the colours directly, Export Mesh writes a glb.\n\nModels: swap the checkpoint and ControlNet for your own (an SDXL union / depth one works). The erosion runs at 512² and is upsampled to 1024² (with a fine relief on top), the generation size, so the masks, the control image and the texture line up pixel for pixel."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
